# Kurin — Cursor Rules

This file is read automatically by Cursor. For the full project guide, see `AGENTS.md`.

## Quick Reference

- **Platform:** iOS 27 (iPhone 17) · watchOS 11 (Apple Watch Series 11)
- **Language:** Swift 6+ · SwiftUI · SwiftData · HealthKit
- **Architecture:** Clean Architecture with Repo + Service layer (no protocols) inside a single target
- **Source of Truth:** `docs/Feature/<feature-id>-<feature-slug>/requirement.md` + `docs/Feature/<feature-id>-<feature-slug>/spec.md`

## Critical Rules (Always Apply)

1. Read `docs/Feature/<feature-id>-<feature-slug>/requirement.md` and `spec.md` before implementing or planning any feature.
2. No force-unwrap (`!`) or `try!` in production code.
3. No business logic in SwiftUI Views — use `@Observable` ViewModels.
4. Repositories and Services are concrete classes — no protocol abstraction.
5. HealthKit permission denial is not a crash — always provide manual fallback.
6. Name tests with AC numbers: `test_AC01_...`, `test_AC02_...`
7. All non-trivial `internal` Service/Repo symbols need `///` DocC comments.
8. ViewModels call Services only; never call Repositories directly.
9. Use `async/await` — no `DispatchQueue` in new code.
10. Store timestamps with device timezone (`TimeZone.current`).
11. Feature planning & doc authoring is led by `@planner` (no build capability); `@builder` executes verified plans.

## Feature Implementation Order

1. `001-onboarding-health-profile`
2. `002-training-plan-dashboard`
3. `003-exercise-session-guidance`
4. `004-rpe-estimation`
5. `005-training-load-workload`
6. `006-daily-training-adjustment`
7. `007-weekly-training-adjustment`

Adjustment outputs from Features 006 and 007 refresh Feature 002.

See `.agents/rules/` and `.agents/skills/` for detailed guidance.
